---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout title="Heid Lab — ERC Starting Grant" scripts={["header.js"]}>
  <main>
    <p class="eyebrow">European Research Council · Since 2024</p>
    <h1>ERC Starting Grant</h1>
    <p>
      “Deep learning of chemical reactions” — awarded to Esther Heid in September
      2024 to develop generative and predictive deep-learning models for chemical
      reactions across gas-phase, organocatalytic, and biocatalytic systems.
    </p>

    <h2>The project</h2>
    <p>
      Predicting how a reaction will proceed — its products, its rate, its
      selectivity — remains one of the hardest problems in computational
      chemistry. The project builds models that learn reaction behavior directly
      from data while staying grounded in mechanism, so that predictions
      generalise beyond the reactions they were trained on.
    </p>
    <p><!-- TODO: project aims in more detail — objectives, work packages, expected outcomes. --></p>

    <h2>Facts</h2>
    <ul class="clean">
      <li>
        <span class="pub-year">Funder</span>
        <strong>European Research Council</strong> — Starting Grant, awarded
        September 2024.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="pub-year">Host institution</span>
        <strong>TU Wien</strong> — Institute of Materials Chemistry.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="pub-year">Principal investigator</span>
        <strong><a href={`${base}/pi`}>Esther Heid</a></strong>
      </li>
      <!-- TODO: add grant number, project acronym, duration (start/end), and budget. -->
      <!-- TODO: add link to the CORDIS project page once available. -->
    </ul>

    <h2>People on the project</h2>
    <p>
      Several group members work on the ERC project — see the
      <a href={`${base}/team`}>Team</a> page.
    </p>
    <p><!-- TODO: list the specific ERC-funded positions and people. --></p>

    <h2>Related publications</h2>
    <p>
      Output from the project appears on the
      <a href={`${base}/publications`}>Publications</a> page.
    </p>
